lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record for Monroe County runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, and September to October came in under 90% of normal in 40 of them on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids. In 2025 the middle saw January to February at 27% of normal and August to September at 34%. So far in 2026, March to April came in at 169% on the middle. Grid 23552 had its driest year in 1988 at 52% of normal.</p>"}
